<h2 id="onlyreftdd-quality" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. TDD delta — Quality bar</h2>

After **`onlyref`** shape is satisfied, **extend the plan’s Quality bar** (or add **“TDD bar”** subsection) with **per-phase** rows. Runner/harness phases also inherit **onlyref** **neatlog** criteria (**.cursor/rules/neatlog-operator-logging-bar.mdc**).

| Column | Content |
|--------|---------|
| **Phase** | Phase number + short name |
| **TDD mode** | **`strict-TDD`** or **`smoke-after-delete`** (see [heuristics](#onlyreftdd-heuristics)) |
| **Test-first artifact** | File path(s) + test name(s) to add **before** production code (fixtures, expected JSON shape, API assertion, Playwright spec) |
| **Red case** | One sentence: what must fail before the impl lands |
| **Green gate** | Command or test subset that must pass before phase `[X]` |

**Rules:**

- **`strict-TDD` phases:** plan must name concrete test file(s) and the contract under test (manifest row count, scope id, API payload field, pool-diff unique keys, etc.).
- **`smoke-after-delete` phases:** plan lists **post-delete smoke tests** only (route 404, grep guard, manifest scope absent, existing suite still green) — no forced red-first test for pure removal.
- Every phase gets **exactly one** TDD mode label in the plan (execution agent must echo it — see **aciubtdd**).

